		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5219&amp;p=37736#p37736"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><br>It's not possible to test a "rubber duckie" in a good way on a VNA or antenna analyzer/swr meter in a proper way.<br>You need to create an earth plane that is similar to the radio including a person who is holding the radio.<br><br>But it's not a perfect match when using the radio normally either, the swr is probably around 3:1 or so on most frequencies.<br><br>I have also tested some duckies on my TinySA but I at least noticed some resonance points where the swr was low.</div></blockquote>That's a good point.  It is the only HT antenna I have that doesn't have at least a 3:1 or better in its intended range, however, which is what made me think there might be a problem there.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8923">KC1VXD</a> — Fri Jul 18, 2025 10:02 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
